Analysis & Estimation
.fcs files were imported and managed in Rstudio using the R package [flowPloidy](https://github.com/plantarum/flowPloidy) (Smith et al., 2018). Using flowPloidy's shiny R interface, which displays data histograms, G1peaks of amphipod and chicken were identified. Chicken G1 peaks were confirmed using the invidulal CRBC sample. Each amphipod sample genome estimation was calculated on non-gated and gated populations. Gated samples were gated using a SSC-H/YL2.H y-axis and YL2.H x-axis where singlet nuclei populations were gated using a rectangular gate. Genome size estimations were conducted on non-gated and gated data, with estimations not significantly differing in size between treatments. Size estimations were found to be around a half gigabyte: .50-.60pg c-value (.48-.59Gb).

